    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404-a1">

                <pb facs="0602" n="508" xml:id="pg508"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 447.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peirce to Mr.
                            Rawicz.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-11-11"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It is a long time since this legation
                    received any news concerning the status of Anton Yablkowski. The last account
                    reported that he could leave the Empire but was forbidden to return, and hoped
                    that by writing he might, through a general amnesty, be permitted to remain.
                    Please inform me at your earliest convenience of the actual status.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert H. D. Peirce</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
